Step 1 — Create a staging table in your control database
Run this while connected to your control database:
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS dbo.COLUMNLIST_STAGING;

CREATE TABLE dbo.COLUMNLIST_STAGING
(
    TABLE_NAME VARCHAR(256),
    COLUMN_NAME VARCHAR(256),
    ORDINAL_POSITION INT
);

Step 2 — Insert the column metadata from PROD
INSERT INTO dbo.COLUMNLIST_STAGING
(
    TABLE_NAME,
    COLUMN_NAME,
    ORDINAL_POSITION
)
SELECT
    TABLE_NAME,
    COLUMN_NAME,
    ORDINAL_POSITION
FROM PROD.INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS
WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA = 'dbo'
  AND TABLE_NAME = 'pat_enc';

Step 3 — Build the comma-separated column list
Now run this in your control database:
SELECT
    STRING_AGG(
        CAST(QUOTENAME(COLUMN_NAME) AS VARCHAR(MAX)),
        ', '
    ) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY ORDINAL_POSITION) AS COLUMNLIST
FROM dbo.COLUMNLIST_STAGING
WHERE TABLE_NAME = 'pat_enc';

If this works, we can use the same approach to update your table inventory.
Step 4 — Update your table inventory
The final update will look like this (replace the example table and key column names with yours):
UPDATE dbo.TABLE_LIST
SET COLUMNLIST =
(
    SELECT
        STRING_AGG(
            CAST(QUOTENAME(COLUMN_NAME) AS VARCHAR(MAX)),
            ', '
        ) WITHIN GROUP (ORDER BY ORDINAL_POSITION)
    FROM dbo.COLUMNLIST_STAGING
    WHERE TABLE_NAME = dbo.TABLE_LIST.SOURCE_TABLE
)
WHERE SOURCE_TABLE = 'pat_enc';
